// An UNBEAMED eighth chord must carry its flag (起票 2026-08-05,
// scratch/ベースタブLy/blogger2.lys, reproduced verbatim). The flag is the STEM's
// grob, indifferent to how many heads hang on it — LilyPond makes one Flag per
// Stem (lily/stem-engraver.cc:152-160) and kills it only for a beamed stem — but
// DrawChord had NO flag branch at all: the voice-two <bes' ges c>8 drew a bare
// down-stem while the voice-one f'8 beside it took the single-note recipe and got
// its flag. Nothing in the corpus wrote an unbeamed flagged chord, so no snapshot
// ever saw the absence; this book holds one flag of each direction (f'8 up, the
// chord down) plus the partial-measure and 3-flat accidental column around them.
// ⚠️ The skyline side (ItemSkylineFactory.AddFlag, now chord-aware to keep draw
// and reserve one fact) has NO binding observer in this book — the down flag ends
// below everything that follows. A book where a chord's flag pushes its neighbour
// still needs writing.
key g major

section A { partial 8 }

part melody {
  section A { voice { f'8 } { <bes' ges c>8 } }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff melody
}
